# The site is served byte-for-byte by GitHub Pages and has no build step, so
# every checkout must be identical. Without this, a Windows machine with
# core.autocrlf=true silently rewrites every file to CRLF on checkout — which
# (a) changes what GitHub Pages serves and (b) breaks the source-scanning test
# suites, whose comment-stripping regex cannot span a trailing \r, so the old
# buggy code quoted inside comments trips every "no live copy of X" assertion.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.svg -text
*.ico binary
